===Alternative forms===

* [[colourise]] {{context|UK}}
* [[colourize]] {{context|UK}}
* [[colorise]] {{context|UK|rare}}

===Etymology===
From ''[[colour]]'' (traditionally reformed to ''[[color]]'' when preceding a Greek suffix) + ''[[-ize]]''.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|coloriz|ing}}

# To add color to.
#: ''The child '''colorized''' the drawing.''
#: ''The woman '''colorized''' her hair.''
# {{photography|filmology}} to convert [[black and white]] media to [[color]] by digital post production, often used in digital photography and in video special effects
#: ''There is a '''colorized''' version of Casablanca.''
#* {{quote-news|year=1988|date=August 26|author=[[w:Jonathan Rosenbaum|Jonathan Rosenbaum]]|title=Looking for America|work=Chicago Reader|url=https://securesite.chireader.com/cgi-bin/Archive/abridged2.bat?path=1988/880826/SENSES
|passage=What we see are beautiful overlapping NASA satellite photographs of the American mainland, {{...|proceeding sequentially from the east to the west--photographs }}taken in black and white and then luminously '''colorized''' by computer for scientific reasons. }}

